1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:07,120
The simplest command, PNG frames to MP4.

2
00:00:07,120 --> 00:00:13,640
What did FFmpeg put in the file?

3
00:00:13,640 --> 00:00:19,550
50 synthetic PNG frames. RGB.

4
00:00:19,550 --> 00:00:27,830
libx264, quality 18, no pixel format flag.

5
00:00:27,830 --> 00:00:36,280
Profile: High 4:4:4 Predictive.

6
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:42,620
Pixel format: yuv444p.

7
00:00:42,620 --> 00:00:53,670
4:2:0 shares color between neighbours.

8
00:00:53,670 --> 00:01:06,930
4:4:4 keeps color for every pixel.

9
00:01:06,930 --> 00:01:15,390
-pix_fmt yuv420p: profile High.

10
00:01:15,390 --> 00:01:28,080
A yuv420p source needs no flag.

11
00:01:28,080 --> 00:01:39,570
PSNR vs the PNG frames, two ffmpeg builds.

12
00:01:39,570 --> 00:01:53,930
The numbers move with the build. The order does not.

13
00:01:53,930 --> 00:01:58,140
One missing flag. A different profile.

14
00:01:58,140 --> 00:02:01,640
Not tested: any specific player.
